<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Headless UI smoke tests (#741), kept in their own project so the fast logic suite stays fast and
    free of an Avalonia application lifetime. These render real views into a headless surface, which is
    the only place a reflection binding or a missing resource actually fails - the app disables compiled
    bindings globally, so those errors exist only at runtime.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>true</TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>
    <RootNamespace>OpenTabletArtist.UiTests</RootNamespace>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Microsoft Testing Platform, not VSTest (#756). xunit v3 test projects are executables that
         host their own runner; TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport tells `dotnet test` to run that host
         instead of going through the VSTest bridge, and OutputType=Exe is what xunit v3 requires once
         Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk is no longer there to set it.

         So xunit.runner.visualstudio, Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and coverlet.collector are gone: the
         first two are the VSTest path, and coverlet.collector is a VSTest data collector that nothing
         collected — no workflow ran with coverage and there is no .runsettings in the tree.

         One gotcha for local use: passing a VSTest filter to `dotnet test` no longer filters anything.
         It warns (MTP0001, "VSTest-specific properties ... will be ignored"), runs the whole suite and
         exits 0, which is easy to miss in a wall of output. Filter by running the test exe directly,
         which takes xunit's own switches:

             bin/Debug/net10.0/<suite>.exe -class Namespace.ClassName
             bin/Debug/net10.0/<suite>.exe -method Namespace.ClassName.MethodName

         CI is unaffected: it runs `dotnet test <csproj>` in its usual no-build form with no filter,
         which works unchanged, and a failing test still exits non-zero (checked, not assumed). -->

    <!-- Avalonia.Headless.XUnit 12.x is built on xunit v3, which is why this project moved there first.
         The logic suite followed (#756), so all three suites now sit on one major and one runner.

         This package is what pins the major: it is compiled against xunit.v3.extensibility.core 3.2.2,
         and 4.x changed TestIntrospectionHelper.GetTestCaseDetails. Its NuGet dependency is a floor,
         not a pin, so restore will happily resolve 4.x and every test then fails at discovery with
         MissingMethodException - a build that warns about nothing. Do not bump past 3.x until Avalonia
         ships a headless package built against xunit.v3 4.x. Checked when the MTP move landed:
         Avalonia.Headless.XUnit 12.1.3, the newest published, still declares 3.2.2.

         #935 no longer waits on that. The flake there was the VSTest adapter rejecting the assembly-
         info JSON after 3.2.2's in-process runner appended a shutdown message to it (xunit/xunit#3576,
         fixed upstream in 4.0.0) - and that adapter is no longer in the path at all, so the failure
         mode is gone rather than mitigated. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Headless.XUnit" Version="12.1.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" Version="3.2.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Shared with the logic suite rather than copied: one fake daemon, so a change to
         IDaemonTransport can't leave two drifting stand-ins behind. -->
    <!-- The library suite owns these now; both app suites compile them from there so there is one copy. -->
    <Compile Include="..\OtdInterop.Tests\MemorySettingsFileStore.cs" Link="MemorySettingsFileStore.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\OtdInterop.Tests\FakeDaemonTransport.cs" Link="FakeDaemonTransport.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\OtdInterop.Tests\NullOtdLog.cs" Link="NullOtdLog.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\OpenTabletArtist\OpenTabletArtist.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
